{"chunk_id": "737e19e9bc61", "text": "When the fiery sage Durvasa arrives during a secret audience between Rama and the personified Death, Lakshmana must choose between obeying Rama\u2019s command not to interrupt and preventing the sage from unleashing a catastrophic curse on the kingdom. Deciding that his own life is worth less than the destruction of all others, Lakshmana interrupts and announces the sage. Rama receives Durvasa and feeds him after his thousand\u2011year fast, but the vow tied to the interrupted meeting forces a terrible consequence. Guided by the counsel of the priest Vasishtha, Rama declares Lakshmana banished\u2014equivalent to death for a man of honor. Accepting fate calmly, Lakshmana goes to the Sarayu, enters deep meditation, and is taken bodily to heaven, revealed as a divine portion of Vishnu.\nBound by a vow after Lakshmana interrupts his meeting with Death, Rama banishes him; Lakshmana meditates by the Sarayu and ascends to heaven.\nThemes: dharma vs affection, vows and duty, sacrifice, divine destiny, ascension", "vector": [0.009862643666565418, -0.02671074867248535, 0.003869669744744897, 0.00411174027249217, -0.004070242401212454, 0.00984189473092556, -0.021509692072868347, -0.008112819865345955, -0.02409638836979866, -0.020486079156398773, 0.026281937956809998, 0.012746740132570267, 0.00658777542412281, 0.020084934309124947, 0.010492026805877686, -0.0034598789643496275, 0.04274273291230202, -0.02495400980114937, 0.035273127257823944, -0.022934449836611748, -0.014607224613428116, -0.02231198363006115, -0.016156475991010666, 0.022104494273662567, -0.02539665251970291, 0.008970440365374088, 0.01049894280731678, -0.0219385027885437, 0.010789427906274796, -0.00947533082216978, -0.005512290634214878, -0.006570484489202499, -0.005844273138791323, -0.0035394164733588696, -0.0340835265815258, -0.003745176363736391, -0.003243744606152177, -0.011121409945189953, 0.010422863997519016, -0.02029242366552353, 0.009413084015250206, -0.004692709539085